{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-208784",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $y$ that satisfy both $y-5\\le 2$ and $2y+7>11$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $y-5\\le 2\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & \\le 2 \\\\ y-5+5 & \\le 2+5 \\\\ y & \\le 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/b0107bec7ccb2c56036de405a29870e8cfcc166cc6405f425fc3296ec8f1be2b.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $2y+7>11\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+7 & >11 \\\\ 2y+7-7 & >11-7 \\\\ 2y & >4 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & >\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ y & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/59523e51144ef776295ec43032def1bc0192351deb6294fbb2d56acd87bb2cac.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $y$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/981477f5336b96998b61b7ab18647609cb33c12984c14049621ac15c698c25a5.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $2<y\\le 7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
